    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes along with the full build. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement: when a request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, allow creating an owner at an address already used by a same-lastName owner, assign both the same stable `householdId`, and return it.\n\nThe \"allow\" half was already implemented in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (it skips the duplicate lastName+address conflict check when `sharesHousehold` is true). I added the `householdId` half:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `householdId` string property to the `Owner` response schema (DTOs are generated from this spec at build time).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` that populates `householdId` from a new deterministic `householdId(owner)` method. It normalizes the last name and address (trim, collapse whitespace, lower-case \u2014 matching the controller's `normalizeHouseholdKey`), joins them, and returns the first 8 upper-case hex chars of the SHA-256.\n\nBecause the id is derived deterministically from normalized lastName+address, every owner in the same household gets the identical, stable identifier automatically \u2014 no DB column, no entity change, and no cross-owner update logic needed. Owners `b` and `c` in the test share `a`'s last name and address, so all three resolve to the same non-blank `householdId`.\n\n`mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
